    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 267 tests pass, including the new Cp08 test. \n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did to make `registrationDate` default to today on owner creation and appear in the response:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto`/`OwnerFieldsDto` gain a `LocalDate registrationDate` field (Jackson serializes it as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) entity field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n- **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 the `POST /api/owners` pipeline's first step now defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the request omits it (an explicitly-supplied date is honored).\n- **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nMapStruct maps the field automatically in both directions (request \u2192 entity, entity \u2192 response) since the names match, so no mapper change was needed.",
